{
  "subtype": "focus_inference",
  "implied_focus": "The clinical nature/type of the patient's presenting concern (categorizing what each visit is about, by body system, episode type, and severity)",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "primary_clinical_object",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Directly types the concern by clinical body-system/category, which is the core of 'main types of concerns' -- the strongest realization of the focus."
    },
    {
      "name": "severity_or_impact",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "A coherent facet of a presenting concern: how serious/impactful it is, differentiating types of concerns along severity."
    },
    {
      "name": "visit_episode_type",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Characterizes the concern as acute/chronic/preventive, a meaningful facet of what type of concern is being presented."
    },
    {
      "name": "acuity_class",
      "supports_focus": false,
      "rationale": "Routine/Urgent/Emergency largely restates the existing 'urgency' column and overlaps with severity; adds little distinct concern-typing signal."
    },
    {
      "name": "clinical_domain",
      "supports_focus": false,
      "rationale": "Department/specialty (General Practice, Pediatrics...) mostly duplicates the existing 'department' column and correlates with primary_clinical_object rather than adding an independent facet of the concern itself."
    }
  ],
  "focus_coherence": 0.82,
  "structure_quality": 0.7,
  "focus_actionability": 0.8,
  "rationale": "The columns collectively center on one coherent, data-inferable focus: characterizing the type of presenting clinical concern. primary_clinical_object, severity_or_impact, and visit_episode_type form a genuine multi-facet decomposition (what/how-severe/what-kind-of-episode) at useful granularity, directly serving the 'main types of concerns' query and giving an analyst actionable categories. Structure quality is dented because acuity_class and clinical_domain are near-duplicates of the pre-existing urgency and department columns and correlate with the primary categorization rather than adding independent, differentiating facets -- so the set is slightly padded with redundant restatements. Overall a solid, actionable focus with a somewhat diluted structure."
}

